% BAB/L/020, Science Museum Group Collection, document aa110001682.
% The cover (222/596): "No 20 continuation of No 19", "31 July 1840"; the
% opened sheet (222/597): two tables, each with its variable cards; the back
% (222/598): faint figures at the top left, nothing of the program. Read from
% the zoom images at full resolution. See sources/notes/L020.md.
%
% DRAFT, not yet in the notation the engine reads (hence .bab.draft, which
% build.rs does not pick up). Two things the engine lacks:
%
%  1. "Give off and retain" in one operation. A column read is written "0"
%     and then, below and to the right, its number again ("0 'B"); its
%     complement is laid in a complement column ("C.'B") and given back in
%     the same operation, leaving that column "0". Written here, as a
%     proposal: `v7 0 B'` (given off and retained) and `v17 CB' 0` (laid and
%     given back). The cards show it: (v7 v17) ... (v17 v7).
%  2. The variable cards themselves, written beside each row as pairs
%     (from, to): (v7 v17) gives v7 to the mill and its complement to v17;
%     (v17 v7) gives it back; (v3 0) gives v3 to the mill and leaves it at
%     zero; (0 v18) puts the mill's result in v18. With each row its number of
%     pairs, a total for each group of three rows (=12, =24 ...), and a
%     running count carried over from No 19 (136, 148, 160 ...). Written
%     here, as a proposal, `Cards` after each row: `Cards (v7 v17)(v3 0)(v17
%     v7)(0 v18) 4`, and `Carried 136`, `Total 148`.
%
% Checked outside the engine (every cell, complement, quantity and card
% count; 126 of 128 agree): see the notes.
%
% The sheet writes accents before the letter ('B, ''B, 'γ); here after (B',
% B'', γ'). Its Greek: γ δ ε, then ∂ (round d) and e for the last equation.

Sheet BAB/L/020
No. 20
Date 31 Jul 1840          "31 July 1840"   % cover
Title "Notation of the Reduction of the Three Equations Bx + Cy + Dz + E = 0, 'Bx + 'Cy + 'Dz + 'E = 0, ''Bx + ''Cy + ''Dz + ''E = 0 to two viz γy + δz + ε = 0, 'γy + 'δz + 'ε = 0 and these to ∂z + e = 0 with the solution"
Image 222/596 cover: "No 20 continuation of No 19"
Image 222/597 the two tables and their cards
Image 222/598 back

Letters B C D E B' C' D' E' B'' C'' D'' E''
Unknowns x y z
Equation B x + C y + D z + E = 0
Equation B' x + C' y + D' z + E' = 0
Equation B'' x + C'' y + D'' z + E'' = 0

% The first table. Columns: "No. of the Opn"; a brace for each group of
% three; "Opn"; "Quant" (the mill's quantity); "Ingress", "Egress" (empty);
% the store under "Bx + Cy + Dz + E = 0": v2 B, v3 C, v4 D, v5 E; under
% "'Bx + 'Cy + 'Dz + 'E = 0": v7 'B, v8 'C, v9 'D, v10 'E; under "''Bx ...":
% v12 ''B, v13 ''C, v14 ''D, v15 ''E; v16 headed "C. B..", v17 "C. 'B..", and
% a third, unheaded complement column; v18 and v19 headed "Prod"; then the
% cards, "Carried over 136" above them.
